{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_codebase_audit", "label": "Codebase Audit 2026-10-04", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_c1_bozo_clone_growth_renderer_crash", "label": "C1 Bozo clone-growth renderer crash (slots 7/8)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "C1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only 18 strand bundles (6 players x 3) existed while gameplay permits 8 seats; fix provisions 8*3 bundles without touching animation math or simulation."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_h1_nikalz_wave_recovery_bypass", "label": "H1 Nikalz waves bypass recovery/escape protection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "H1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wave eligibility used isActive/isInvulnerable and skipped the shared direct-hit recovery policy; fix makes PeriodicHit return whether a reaction applied and writes Nikalz private stun only when allowed, keeping damage and 120/360-frame stun durations."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_m1_bee_swarm_population_limit", "label": "M1 Bee swarm population limit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "M1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "BeeSwarm had no expiry or capacity, growing collision work and rollback snapshots; a deterministic cap of 100 swarms per owner replacing the oldest was chosen as a resource-safety policy, not a balance value, and no expiry timer was added."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_m2_dodo_simultaneous_pulse_trades", "label": "M2 Dodo simultaneous lethal pulse trades", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "M2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "advanceDodo applied damage immediately so earlier seats suppressed later casters' pulses; fix collects contacts before committing damage, matching the shared continuous-attack system."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_m3_match_end_cleanup_nikalz_entities", "label": "M3 Match-end cleanup omits Nikalz entities", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "M3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Life cleanup cleared projectiles/hazards/clones/structures but not bees/waves, and advanceNikalz cleanup was unreachable after advanceFrame's result return; shared CombatLifecycle.clearCombatEntities now covers knockouts, tournament forfeits and elimination endings."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_m4_clone_growth_dispose_ownership", "label": "M4 Clone-growth visual dispose ownership", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "M4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SceneRenderer.dispose traversed mesh materials but never called HairCloneGrowth.dispose, leaking owned textures; fix calls cloneGrowth.dispose and detaches root before generic traversal."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_m5_regression_suite_failures", "label": "M5 Six unresolved regression failures", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "M5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Balance/art/architecture changes were not reconciled with fixtures; only the 19 stale movement-facing baseline entries were updated after verifying zero trace changes. Never blindly regenerate golden hashes."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_m6_shared_systems_character_identity", "label": "M6 Shared systems retain character identities", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "M6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HairSystem hard-coded characterId==='bozo' and lifecycle policy was duplicated; narrow repair moves companion health ratio/offset into validated character definitions and shares terminal cleanup instead of rewriting combat."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_l1_hazard_damage_attribution", "label": "L1 Hazard damage attribution uses burn owner", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Burn and generic hazard damage shared a helper with burn-specific metadata; generic hazard events now carry the hazard's owner and move."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_l2_finished_room_timeout_exemption", "label": "L2 Finished-room timeout exemption", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": "L2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Clients could claim a finished frame to keep a room exempt from inactivity expiry; rooms now expire 15 minutes after the first finish claim and repeats cannot extend retention."}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_all_roster_replay_test", "label": "All-roster replay/invariant test (256 pairings)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/codebase-audit-2026-10-04.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_codebase_audit_2026_10_04_combatlifecycle_clearcombatentities", "label": "CombatLifecycle.clearCo